Falsifies `current_cpu_contract::verification::the_readers_answer_only_what_the_page_holds`.

The defect: the reader's bound check is off by one, so an id equal to `CPU_ID_BOUND` is handed back
and indexes one past the end of a per-core array.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(page.cpu(), None)`, on a word equal to `CPU_ID_BOUND`.

diff --git a/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
index 5fbeb834b..7c4b6f85d 100644
--- a/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/current_cpu_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -344,7 +344,7 @@ impl CurrentCpuPage {
     pub fn cpu(&self) -> Option<usize> {
         match self.word(CPU_OFFSET)? {
             UNSCHEDULED => None,
-            cpu if cpu >= CPU_ID_BOUND as u64 => None,
+            cpu if cpu > CPU_ID_BOUND as u64 => None,
             cpu => Some(cpu as usize),
         }
     }
